{
 "primitive": "4. Statement",
 "about": "A statement is what a seal stamps: one JSON object whose RFC 8785 bytes are fingerprinted and kept. It names its form in 'form', a name of the shape imprint.thing/version. Wherever it points at something it uses a reference, an object with exactly 'fingerprint' and 'over': the fingerprint in its one spelling, and 'over' as 'bytes', 'rfc8785' or a form name. A fingerprint never stands as a plain string. It holds no fraction (a decimal is a string) and no whole number past 2^53. 'stated_at', where present, is the issuer's own clock: UTC to the second, ending in Z. No member name starts with U+0000. Everything else is the issuer's own.",
